        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "7c1c163b-6cd5-5f50-ac8e-3b4c5686621b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Junkers Flugzeug- und Motorenwerke AG (Junkers)\n- Products: Pirna 014\n- People: Former Junkers engineers\n- Places: East Germany (GDR), Soviet Union, Dessau, Germany\n\nFacts:\n- Junkers Flugzeug- und Motorenwerke AG, also known as Junkers and earlier as JCO or JKO during World War I, was a major German aircraft and aircraft engine manufacturer based in Dessau, Germany.\n- Junkers produced many innovative and well-known airplanes during its more than fifty years of history in Dessau, Germany.\n- Former Junkers engineers were held in custody in the Soviet Union after World War II and were repatriated to East Germany in 1954.\n- The Pirna 014 was an axial turbojet designed in East Germany in the mid- to late 1950s by former Junkers engineers.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "49e63fd9-9139-5e96-ab9c-e927dc4f8841",
        "text": "Page: Pirna 014. Sentence: The Pirna 014 was an axial turbojet designed in East Germany (or the GDR) in the mid- to late 1950s by former Junkers engineers, who were repatriated to East Germany in 1954 after being held in custody in the Soviet Union following World War II.\nPage: Junkers. Sentence: Junkers Flugzeug- und Motorenwerke AG (JFM, earlier JCO or JKO in World War I), more commonly Junkers, was a major German aircraft and aircraft engine manufacturer.\nPage: Junkers. Sentence: It produced some of the world's most innovative and best-known airplanes over the course of its fifty-plus year history in Dessau, Germany.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
